# TED - Edit text on screen

```text
B0:TED D0:NOTES.TXT
```

## Start the editor

TED uses the ANSI personality and an 80-by-24 screen backend. Select
ANSISCRN on cpmsim, M4SCRN on Model 4, or M2SCRN on Model II. Check RSX
LIST first. On cpmsim, after unloading any conflicting personality:

```text
RSX LOAD ANSISCRN
RSX LOAD ANSI
B0:TED D0:NOTES.TXT
```

## Edit and save

At TED>, S enters screen mode. Ctrl-S/D moves left/right, Ctrl-E/X moves
up/down, and Ctrl-V switches between overwrite and insert. Ctrl-Z
returns to command mode. For a named file, W at TED> writes the document
and EX exits. In screen mode Ctrl-K then S saves and continues. TED.TXT
on the Utilities disk lists the editing keys.
